let __v_603 = pyrt::literals::decode("{\"$dict\":[[\"water\",{\"$dict\":[[\"names\",{\"$tuple\":[\"bottle of water\",\"bottled water\",\"pack of water\",\"case of water\",\"water in a shop\",\"still water\",\"sparkling water\"]}],[\"reply\",\"A 500ml bottle of water is about £1 in a shop and £2 or more at a station, while a 6-pack of 1.5 litre bottles is about £3 to £4 in a supermarket. Tap water is the same stuff and costs nothing, so the bottle is for the day out.\"]]}],[\"cheese\",{\"$dict\":[[\"names\",{\"$tuple\":[\"cheese\",\"block of cheese\",\"block of cheddar\",\"cheddar\",\"400g of cheese\",\"packet of cheese\"]}],[\"reply\",\"A 400g block of cheddar is about £3.50 to £5, and the same weight of a named farmhouse one £4 to £6. Mature costs a little more than mild, and the deli counter is dearer than the block.\"]]}],[\"butter\",{\"$dict\":[[\"names\",{\"$tuple\":[\"butter\",\"block of butter\",\"packet of butter\",\"tub of butter\"]}],[\"reply\",\"A 250g block of butter is about £2.20 to £3, and a tub of spread about £1.50. Own-brand butter is the cheapest, and it freezes well, so buy it when it is on offer.\"]]}],[\"pasta\",{\"$dict\":[[\"names\",{\"$tuple\":[\"pasta\",\"bag of pasta\",\"packet of pasta\",\"spaghetti\",\"penne\"]}],[\"reply\",\"A 500g bag of dried pasta is about 75p to £1.50, and a fresh one £2 to £3. Dried is a fifth of the price a portion, and the shape does not change the price much.\"]]}],[\"rice\",{\"$dict\":[[\"names\",{\"$tuple\":[\"rice\",\"bag of rice\",\"kilo of rice\",\"basmati\",\"long grain rice\"]}],[\"reply\",\"A kilo of long-grain rice is about £1 to £2.50 and a kilo of basmati £2 to £3.50. It keeps for months in a cupboard, so the bigger bag is usually the better buy.\"]]}],[\"bacon\",{\"$dict\":[[\"names\",{\"$tuple\":[\"bacon\",\"pack of bacon\",\"packet of bacon\",\"rashers\",\"smoked bacon\"]}],[\"reply\",\"A 300g pack of bacon is about £2.50 to £4. Dry-cured costs more than the kind that is pumped with water, which shrinks in the pan, and the 2-for deals are usually the cheapest way to buy it.\"]]}],[\"salmon\",{\"$dict\":[[\"names\",{\"$tuple\":[\"salmon\",\"salmon fillets\",\"side of salmon\",\"piece of salmon\"]}],[\"reply\",\"Two salmon fillets are about £5 to £7, and a whole side £15 to £25. The frozen fillets are often half the price of the fresh counter for the same fish.\"]]}],[\"bananas\",{\"$dict\":[[\"names\",{\"$tuple\":[\"bananas\",\"banana\",\"bunch of bananas\"]}],[\"reply\",\"Bananas are about 15p to 25p each, so a bunch of five is roughly £1. Loose ones are cheaper than a pre-packed bag, and the ripe ones on the reduce shelf are the bargain.\"]]}],[\"apples\",{\"$dict\":[[\"names\",{\"$tuple\":[\"apples\",\"apple\",\"bag of apples\"]}],[\"reply\",\"Six apples are about £1.50 to £2.50 and a kilo about £2. Loose ones let you pick the size, and a bag of the smaller ones is usually the cheapest way.\"]]}],[\"tomatoes\",{\"$dict\":[[\"names\",{\"$tuple\":[\"tomatoes\",\"tomato\",\"pack of tomatoes\",\"punnet of tomatoes\",\"cherry tomatoes\"]}],[\"reply\",\"A 400g pack of salad tomatoes is about £1 to £2, and a punnet of cherry ones £1.50 to £2.50. Loose ones are usually cheaper than a punnet, and in August they are half the winter price.\"]]}],[\"mince\",{\"$dict\":[[\"names\",{\"$tuple\":[\"mince\",\"beef mince\",\"pack of mince\",\"minced beef\"]}],[\"reply\",\"500g of beef mince is about £4 to £6, with the 5% fat one a pound or two more than the 20%. Turkey and pork mince are cheaper, and a bigger pack is usually the better price a kilo.\"]]}],[\"sausages\",{\"$dict\":[[\"names\",{\"$tuple\":[\"sausages\",\"sausage\",\"pack of sausages\",\"pork sausages\"]}],[\"reply\",\"Six to eight sausages are about £2.50 to £4, and a butcher's £4 to £6. The cheapest are mostly rusk and water, so read the meat percentage on the pack.\"]]}],[\"cereal\",{\"$dict\":[[\"names\",{\"$tuple\":[\"cereal\",\"box of cereal\",\"cornflakes\",\"box of cornflakes\",\"muesli\"]}],[\"reply\",\"A box of cereal is about £2 to £3.50, and the shop's own version of a branded one about half the price. A big bag of own-brand flakes is the cheapest breakfast there is a bowl.\"]]}],[\"yoghurt\",{\"$dict\":[[\"names\",{\"$tuple\":[\"yoghurt\",\"yogurt\",\"pot of yoghurt\",\"tub of yoghurt\",\"greek yoghurt\"]}],[\"reply\",\"A four-pack of yoghurt is about £1.50 to £2.50, and a 1kg tub £2 to £3, which is much cheaper a portion. Greek-style costs more than natural, and the big tub is the one to buy if you eat it every day.\"]]}],[\"peas\",{\"$dict\":[[\"names\",{\"$tuple\":[\"peas\",\"frozen peas\",\"bag of peas\",\"kilo of peas\"]}],[\"reply\",\"A kilo of frozen peas is about £1.50 to £2 and lasts months. Fresh peas in season are sweeter but cost three or four times as much for a much smaller bag.\"]]}]]}")?;
